SamIAm <not@realaddress.net> wrote:

>What is a ttyrec?  

A complete recording of a sequence of textual screen displays, such as
the output of NetHack in text mode.

> What program opens it?  

Several. For example, ipbt. (Although the homepage at
http://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/ipbt/ states that it is for
Unix, it can easily be compiled under Cygwin for Windows.)

>What is its purpose? 

View recordings of particular strategies (such as "How to kill Master
Kaen") or complete games of skillful players to learn their techniques.

